  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The abstract outlines a conceptual framework and policy context rather than presenting empirical findings, case study evaluations, or quantitative performance metrics.",
      "what": "This paper introduces 'Tree Value Visions', a framework designed to help local authorities integrate relational values and multispecies justice into urban forest management. It addresses the challenge of balancing competing policy objectives—such as carbon sequestration, biodiversity, flood regulation, and public health—under the spatial and resource constraints of urban areas.",
      "why": "It provides planners and developers with a structured approach to make evidence-led decisions on nature-based solutions, moving beyond simple tree-planting targets to consider broader ecological and social justice outcomes."
    }
